  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "note-light",
      "page": "page-3",
      "x": 1960,
      "y": 40,
      "w": 280,
      "text": "LIGHT THEME (overcast daylight)\nToken mapping per DESIGN.md: bg #F5F6F8, cards white, ink #1A2028, taillight #D63A26, headlight #0E7FA6, warn #B06E10. Accents use the darker light-theme values for WCAG contrast on white. Photo/camera areas stay dark (they are photographs). Six representative screens - the rest follow the same mapping mechanically."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-chosen",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 1470,
      "y": 40,
      "w": 300,
      "text": "CHOSEN SET (Aug 2026)\nHome C (Garage-first) · Confirm A (Sheet over photo) · Trends B (Tile grid).\n\nNew screens follow the same language:\n- Welcome: guest first-launch, no account, two paths (add car / import).\n- Reminders: date and/or odometer based, amber only for 'needs attention', progress toward due.\n- Edit entry: same DIN block + verified line as Confirm; edits recalc consumption; delete is quiet text, red lives only in the system confirm dialog. Now carries the sync-safety row: 'Changed by sync - Restore my version' (SYNC.md S1).\n- Recently deleted: 30-day undo log for deleted entries plus versions overwritten by sync; restored entries rejoin stats."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-unchosen",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 1960,
      "y": 40,
      "w": 260,
      "text": "Kept for reference. Ideas worth stealing later: Home A's big hero metric could become the Trends header; Confirm B's giant readout could be a landscape/one-hand mode of the confirm sheet."
    },
    {
      "id": "note-agent",
      "page": "page-4",
      "x": 980,
      "y": 1060,
      "w": 420,
      "text": "THE CAR AGENT (v2, Pro) - docs/AGENT.md\nDecided 2026-08-29. The tab bar gains a fifth slot: Log · Trends · ● Capture · Ask · Garage. Ask is glyph-and-label, never raised, never accented. Everyone sees the tab; free users land on the examples + the Pro card (AgentAsk).\n\nFour rules every screen here obeys: figures are the app's own numbers rendered as cards, never model prose · every write is a pre-filled form the user saves (AgentReminderDraft) · Ask is never the only door to anything · offline / not-Pro / quota are states with next steps, not errors.\n\nDiagnosis (AgentDiagnosis): context card first, ranked causes each labelled 'from your log' or 'general knowledge', a fixed urgency row (amber only for 'book this week', system red only for 'stop driving').\n\nRU tab label 'Спросить' must be verified at Dynamic Type XL; 'Чат' is the fallback."
    }
  ],
  "launch": {
    "view": "canvas",
